<properties>
    <property id="autoLapEnabled" type="boolean">true</property>
    <!-- Grade-adjusted-speed multiplier (see
         ActivityController.updateGradeAndGap()). Raised from the original
         5.0 guess after fitting HR(t+30s) ~ speed + grade against two real
         rides (skating-only seconds, |grade| outliers beyond 15% dropped as
         GPS/altitude noise): the fitted coefficient came out around 33-44,
         well above the settings.xml slider's current max of 20, with grade
         explaining ~15x more HR variance than speed alone (R^2 0.12 vs
         0.008). Set to 20 (the slider ceiling) rather than the raw fitted
         value: the rider only started pumping symmetrically a couple of
         rides ago, so that estimate likely reflects still-developing
         technique and should trend down, not up, as it improves. Revisit
         once more rides are in and the per-ride estimates stop drifting. -->
    <property id="gradeAdjustCoefficient" type="float">20.0</property>
</properties>
